WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:03.710
Hi, welcome back to Part Three of Nagarjuna.

00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:05.883
We've reached Chapter 15,

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.740
titled "An Inquiry into the Nature of Things."

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:13.450
In Western Chinese languages, we see

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:15.130
it here as RANG BZHIN BRTAG PA

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:17.560
RANG BZHIN BRTAG PA

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:20.781
BRTAG PA meaning PARIKSHA, which means...

00:00:20.781 --> 00:00:21.791
—[female voice] Research —A

00:00:21.791 --> 00:00:23.360
study.

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:25.394
RANG BZHIN is an interesting word

00:00:25.394 --> 00:00:28.210
because it means "its own surface."

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:30.055
BZHIN here means surface.

00:00:30.055 --> 00:00:32.330
BZHIN RAS means surface.

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:35.060
So RANG BZHIN refers to the
"surface" of something. It

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:39.040
means nature, meaning... Let's

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:41.710
make it clear from the beginning, shall we?

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:46.486
It refers to the characteristics of things: their inherent nature,

00:00:46.486 --> 00:00:50.012
a certain quality inherent in things.

00:00:50.012 --> 00:00:52.430
So you have to have this feeling...

00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:55.580
We are going to explore, for example,

00:00:55.580 --> 00:01:00.090
whether fire has a characteristic or inherent nature that it

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:04.380
can generate heat, and then this nature will be activated

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:06.980
and expressed in the world.

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:11.860
Is the inherent nature of fire heat?

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:13.900
Then, for some reason, it went viral and spread

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:16.110
.

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:18.770
Does it have its own unique characteristics?

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:21.130
So when we talk about nature

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:25.820
or self-nature (svabhava) here,
RANG BZHIN, think about it,

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:28.540
this is a thing deep within things,

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:30.080
this is its true nature,

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:32.160
think about its nature.

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:35.700
Okay, now let's look at our argument.

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:39.250
First passage,

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:41.629
verse 1.5: ,

00:01:41.629 --> 00:01:42.987
RANG BZHIN RGYU DANG RKYEN LAS NI, ,

00:01:42.987 --> 00:01:46.478
'BYUNG BAR RIGS PA MA YIN NO, ,

00:01:46.478 --> 00:01:48.620
RGYU DANG RKYEN LAS BYUNG BA YI,

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:51.753
,RANG BZHIN BYAS PA CAN DU 'GYUR,

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:54.720
If you think carefully,

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:57.820
if the characteristics of something are part of it,

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:00.758
it doesn't need to be created.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:07.510
If the characteristics of an object are inherent in itself—

00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:10.070
that is, the meaning of characteristics—

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:12.110
they should not be something you only receive when something else happens

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:15.131
.

00:02:15.131 --> 00:02:17.075
It must be something you're born with.  It's something you're

00:02:17.075 --> 00:02:18.160
born with.

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:20.094
No need to heat the fire.

00:02:20.094 --> 00:02:22.066
[Rubbing hands together]

00:02:22.066 --> 00:02:23.590
Fire is inherently hot.

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:26.950
So if you have to do something first to make the

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:30.583
fire hot, then heat is not the nature of fire.

00:02:31.642 --> 00:02:33.923
—Do you agree?  --agree.

00:02:33.923 --> 00:02:36.590
If other things need to be done,

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:40.360
if another fire must be lit below the fire
to make it hot,

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:42.440
then the nature of fire—

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:44.880
we would not say that heat is the nature of fire.

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:48.710
Therefore, we can say that nature or characteristics

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:50.480
come from the things themselves,

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:52.430
rather than being qualities that only appear when other things exist or when

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:54.000
other causes or conditions exist

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:57.283
.

00:02:57.283 --> 00:02:59.341
,RANG BZHIN RGYU DANG RKYEN LAS NI,

00:02:59.341 --> 00:03:02.166
,'BYUNG BAR RIGS PA MA YIN NO,

00:03:02.166 --> 00:03:07.100
This is inappropriate.
If the existence of the inherent characteristics of something

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:09.390
requires the occurrence of other things, there

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:12.090
must be some cause or condition.

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:14.040
,RGYU DANG RKYEN LAS GANGS BYUNG BA YI,

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:16.865
,RANG BZHIN BYAS PA CAN DU 'GYUR,

00:03:16.865 --> 00:03:21.865
Because the nature of what is caused by other factors or causes

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:26.840
is artificial,

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:29.856
and the meaning of artificial is the opposite of that of nature.

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:36.070
They were put together and then thrown into the fire.

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:38.480
Oh, come here, let me heat it up for you.
[Rubbing hands together]

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:40.160
Then the fire gets hot.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:44.450
Then the nature of fire would not
exist in fire itself.

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:47.630
That would have been created by humans
and then given to fire.

00:03:47.630 --> 00:03:49.934
Okay, do you understand?

00:03:49.934 --> 00:03:51.050
RANG BZHIN BYAS PA CAN

00:03:51.050 --> 00:03:53.393
Therefore, BYAS PA CAN here refers to something that is

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:56.850
almost man-made or created.

00:03:58.225 --> 00:04:03.225
In the jewelry industry, there are real
rubies and sapphires,

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:05.783
as well as fakes.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:09.260
But when people learned to
create real

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:12.980
rubies and sapphires in the laboratory,
there was a great debate about

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:15.110
whether they should be called artificial stones.

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:17.280
Those who succeeded in the process argued that

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:19.320
it was not man-made, but real.

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:21.020
Another person argued that if it wasn't
dug out of the soil and rocks, then it was

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:22.690
n't real.

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:26.411
So they reached a compromise, which they
called "making rubies".  It

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:32.790
sounds better than artificial products or substitutes.

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:37.410
So this was created,
not natural.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:39.283
This is the key point.

00:04:40.842 --> 00:04:43.360
RANG BZHIN BYAS PA CAN ZHES BYAR

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:48.330
If the nature or characteristics of something

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:50.912
must be created from the outside,

00:04:50.912 --> 00:04:52.310
JI LTAR BUR NA RUNG BAR 'GYUR

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:55.210
Then how can it be said to be nature?

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:57.740
It is man-made, created.  Do you

00:04:57.740 --> 00:04:58.910
understand?

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:01.410
It's like making a ruby.

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:02.800
good.

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:04.560
Nagarjuna Bodhisattva...

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:05.970
This is a story.  There's

00:05:05.970 --> 00:05:08.220
a story behind this photo.

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:12.273
My teacher, as I've told you,
I served as his volunteer for

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:18.300
30 years, and for about 25 of those years

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:23.300
I was his driver, taking him between
New Jersey and Washington, D.C.

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:25.920
That's a five-hour drive.

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:27.700
He used to teach there once a month.

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:32.523
So I've done it over 300 times.

00:05:34.485 --> 00:05:35.730
I drove him there.

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:38.160
If we count the round trips, there are a total of 600 trips.

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:42.430
So I know those routes by heart,
and I really enjoy driving him.

00:05:42.430 --> 00:05:46.000
Because he always refuses to answer my questions.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:49.220
He couldn't refuse in the car.

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:52.565
He was locked in the car for five hours,

00:05:52.565 --> 00:05:55.730
and the car he ordered didn't have a radio,

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:58.707
so I couldn't listen to the radio.

00:05:58.707 --> 00:06:01.667
Ordering a car without a radio
requires an extra fee.

00:06:01.667 --> 00:06:03.069
[Laughter]

00:06:03.069 --> 00:06:06.353
In short, all we can do is discuss Buddhism.

00:06:06.353 --> 00:06:08.655
Sometimes he would pretend to be asleep.

00:06:08.655 --> 00:06:11.367
I would say I know you're not asleep.

00:06:11.367 --> 00:06:13.190
Then he...
[imitates snoring]

00:06:13.190 --> 00:06:18.190
Anyway, he always stops at Howard Johnson's restaurant in front of the Delaware Bridge, which is located at the
intersection of Maryland and Delaware

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:21.083


00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:23.840
.

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:26.010
We always stopped at the same spot, and

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:28.630
he would order tea.  As

00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:30.110
you know, he loves drinking tea.

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:32.930
He drinks about 15 cups of tea a day.

00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:36.367
I make him 15-20 cups of tea a day.

00:06:36.367 --> 00:06:40.245
They will try to provide him with creamer.

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:43.160
He would say, “No, I want cream.”

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:45.218
“That’s creamer, I don’t want creamer.

00:06:45.218 --> 00:06:48.460
I want cream, I want the real thing.”

00:06:48.460 --> 00:06:50.110
He taught me these words:

00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:53.080
artificial, fake, unnatural.

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:57.570
Everything I learned from him, including
my own use of words, has a

00:06:57.570 --> 00:06:58.870
structure.

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:00.910
We were sitting somewhere, and he said,

00:07:00.910 --> 00:07:03.285
“This is called BCOS MA.”

00:07:03.285 --> 00:07:04.326
BCOS MA stands for BYAS PA.

00:07:04.326 --> 00:07:06.750
BYAS PA means that it must be
created from the outside world.

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:09.240
This is not natural.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:10.884
good.

00:07:10.884 --> 00:07:13.075
He hates this stuff, he

00:07:13.942 --> 00:07:15.025
really does.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:17.363
good.

00:07:19.810 --> 00:07:22.545
Next paragraph.  It is actually only half a section.

00:07:23.970 --> 00:07:25.657
This is actually RANG LUGS.

00:07:25.657 --> 00:07:27.603
What does that mean?

00:07:27.603 --> 00:07:30.069
This is our argument.

00:07:30.069 --> 00:07:32.044
,RANG BZHIN DAG NI BCOS MIN DANG,

00:07:32.044 --> 00:07:34.490
,GZHAN LA LTOS PA MED PA YIN,

00:07:34.490 --> 00:07:38.320
If it is a real characteristic, it

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:40.398
should not be BCOS MA.

00:07:40.398 --> 00:07:43.990
BCOS MA means man-made or
artificial creation.  It should


00:07:43.990 --> 00:07:46.050
n't taste like creamer.  It

00:07:46.050 --> 00:07:48.248
must be true.

00:07:48.248 --> 00:07:50.983
BCOS MIN means non-creative.

00:07:50.983 --> 00:07:55.020
What is the famous BCOS PA in the Stages of the Path?

00:07:56.522 --> 00:07:58.640
BCOS MA? It

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:00.206
means

00:08:00.206 --> 00:08:03.060
trying to feel like a Bodhisattva when you are not yet one.
[Laughter]

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:05.060
That's good, BCOS MA.

00:08:05.060 --> 00:08:07.493
Good.  A fake Bodhisattva.  The

00:08:08.570 --> 00:08:09.920
Bodhisattva created.

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:13.591
Artificial, you pretend to be a bodhisattva,

00:08:13.591 --> 00:08:16.885
but then you still mess around all day, and things like that.

00:08:16.885 --> 00:08:18.170
,GZHAN LA LTOS PA MED PA YIN,

00:08:18.170 --> 00:08:20.800
If it is the true nature, it

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:23.190
should not need to rely on any

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:25.360
external conditions to exist.

00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:28.590
If fire is inherently hot,

00:08:28.590 --> 00:08:31.280
then it

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:33.430
doesn't matter where the fire is or what happens to it.

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:35.103
He should be warm from the inside out.

00:08:35.103 --> 00:08:36.700
Like this.

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:39.348
This is our definition of nature.

00:08:40.420 --> 00:08:44.590
I was thinking, maybe you
could consider it.

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:47.468
Is this BTAGS PA MTHA'
BZUNG GI RIGS PA?

00:08:47.468 --> 00:08:49.670
Is this BTAGS PA MTHA'
BZUNG GI RIGS PA?

00:08:49.670 --> 00:08:52.230
This is a very, very useful expression.

00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:55.500
I remember once I was debating Buddhist scriptures

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:57.440
at Drepung Monastery.

00:08:57.440 --> 00:09:01.740
I heard this statement, BTAGS
PA MTHA' BZUNG GI RIGS PA.

00:09:01.740 --> 00:09:05.320
BTAGS PA MTHA' BZUNG GI RIGS
PA, means theoretical argument.

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:06.260
Theoretical case studies.

00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:10.350
In theoretical cases, the nature of things

00:09:10.350 --> 00:09:13.917
should possess two qualities.  What is it?

00:09:13.917 --> 00:09:16.330
BCOS MIN
should not be artificially created; it

00:09:16.330 --> 00:09:19.050
should be GZHAN LA LTOS PA MED PA.

00:09:19.050 --> 00:09:20.450
It should not

00:09:22.441 --> 00:09:24.700
depend on other conditions.

00:09:24.700 --> 00:09:28.620
So, does such an inherent property exist?

00:09:28.620 --> 00:09:30.413
This is another debate, you know?

00:09:30.413 --> 00:09:34.221
Theoretically speaking, we said
theoretically, right?

00:09:34.221 --> 00:09:36.120
Theoretically speaking, that's just how it is.  Do

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:39.370
you know if
such a thing actually exists?  We don't know.

00:09:40.333 --> 00:09:45.308
Lama Qiuni also expressed his views.

00:09:46.430 --> 00:09:49.240
This is a very traditional and ancient view

00:09:49.240 --> 00:09:52.870
about what nature should be like if it truly exists
, and that it

00:09:52.870 --> 00:09:54.310
should possess three qualities.

00:09:54.310 --> 00:09:55.730
Get ready.

00:09:55.730 --> 00:09:57.171
First.

00:09:58.682 --> 00:09:59.515
GNYUG MA'I NGO BO

00:09:59.515 --> 00:10:00.348
GNYUG MA'I NGO BO

00:10:01.437 --> 00:10:04.120
GNYUG MA is a very, very rare and

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:09.120
important word, meaning since beginningless time

00:10:09.253 --> 00:10:10.650
[laughter].

00:10:10.650 --> 00:10:12.002
GNYUG MA

00:10:12.002 --> 00:10:12.940
sounds like SMYUG MA,

00:10:12.940 --> 00:10:16.016
which means "bamboo shoot," but it doesn't.

00:10:16.016 --> 00:10:18.700
GNYUG MA means original,

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:21.961
primitive, from the very beginning.

00:10:21.961 --> 00:10:24.860
GNYUG MAGNYUG MA'I NGO BO

00:10:24.860 --> 00:10:29.030
If this is the nature of fire,

00:10:29.030 --> 00:10:32.830
then this nature will always exist within fire.  Do you

00:10:32.830 --> 00:10:33.911
understand?

00:10:33.911 --> 00:10:36.332
It refers to heat, intense heat.

00:10:36.332 --> 00:10:38.380


00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:43.380
If fire has an inherent nature, then
that nature or characteristic

00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:46.150
will remain forever within those things

00:10:46.150 --> 00:10:49.370
as long as fire exists.

00:10:49.370 --> 00:10:51.200
That's the first point.

00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:53.820
Fire is always hot.

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:55.753
Second point.

00:10:56.990 --> 00:11:01.680
Whether you're discussing fire a hundred years ago,

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:03.930
fire a hundred years from now,

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:08.263
or the fire in this room right now, it
should remain unchanged.

00:11:09.130 --> 00:11:11.420
Features will always exist.

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:14.510
Whether you're talking about fire a hundred years from now,

00:11:14.510 --> 00:11:15.840
fire a hundred years ago,

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:18.003
or fire right now, the

00:11:19.260 --> 00:11:21.883
characteristics of fire remain.

00:11:22.850 --> 00:11:24.480
hot.

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:25.513
Third point.

00:11:27.230 --> 00:11:31.300
Its properties should not depend on

00:11:31.300 --> 00:11:35.190
other sources.

00:11:35.190 --> 00:11:37.790
He also gave an interesting example.

00:11:37.790 --> 00:11:41.398
You don't need to put a kettle on the stove.

00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:46.100
Veronica and I recently
got something really cool that

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:47.430
someone gave us.

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:49.913
Was it a cherry pit?

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:53.043
It was in a bag?

00:11:54.340 --> 00:11:57.360
It also contains lavender flowers.

00:11:57.360 --> 00:12:00.530
Put it in the microwave to heat it up,

00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:01.880
and then lie on it.  It's

00:12:01.880 --> 00:12:04.220
very comfortable to sleep like this.  It

00:12:04.220 --> 00:12:07.529
will stay warm for about half an hour, then

00:12:07.529 --> 00:12:10.026
gradually cool down, and you can lie down on it and fall asleep.

00:12:10.026 --> 00:12:12.601
It is very comfortable.

00:12:14.069 --> 00:12:17.180
It looks a bit like a kettle.

00:12:17.180 --> 00:12:18.463
In short, Lama Qiuni said that

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:24.208
if the heat of the fire comes from within, there is

00:12:24.208 --> 00:12:26.768
no need to

00:12:26.768 --> 00:12:28.723
heat the fire with a kettle.

00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:34.520
This is a pillow filled with cherry pits and
lavender.

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:37.850
If you don't need to microwave a cherry pit lavender pillow to

00:12:37.850 --> 00:12:40.180
warm yourself up,

00:12:40.180 --> 00:12:44.319
you might just be naturally warm.  Do you

00:12:44.319 --> 00:12:46.053
understand?

00:12:46.053 --> 00:12:47.150
These are the three key elements.

00:12:47.150 --> 00:12:50.150
Once again, this might be BTAGS
PA MTHA' BZUNG GI RIGS PA.

00:12:50.150 --> 00:12:54.203
In the photo, a woman is about to touch the candlelight.

00:12:55.090 --> 00:12:57.650
You might say something like...

00:12:58.630 --> 00:13:00.180
You might automatically think, "

00:13:00.180 --> 00:13:02.600
I hope she doesn't put her fingers in the fire

00:13:02.600 --> 00:13:04.300
because it will burn her."

00:13:04.300 --> 00:13:06.960
Its nature is to be hot.

00:13:06.960 --> 00:13:08.723
Okay, next paragraph.

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:18.730
These are some other thoughts on the features.

00:13:21.450 --> 00:13:24.863
You should know that my
main ideas about characteristics are those three elements,

00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:29.290
but let's talk about other things together.

00:13:29.290 --> 00:13:31.790
Let's talk about other features

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:34.822
regarding the concept of characteristics.

00:13:34.822 --> 00:13:36.196
,RANG BZHIN YOD PA MA YIN NA,

00:13:36.196 --> 00:13:38.810
,GZHAN GYI DNGOS PO GA LA YOD,

00:13:40.610 --> 00:13:42.415
It is very complicated.

00:13:43.480 --> 00:13:47.620
If you think about it carefully, fire has two natures.

00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:52.093
One originates from within, the other from without.

00:13:53.960 --> 00:13:56.390
For example, the color of fire.  "

00:13:56.390 --> 00:14:00.523
Originating from the outside world" means "
depending on the external environment".

00:14:01.702 --> 00:14:04.240
So which chemical component is it that

00:14:04.240 --> 00:14:06.350


00:14:06.350 --> 00:14:08.330
causes the flame to have a different color?

00:14:08.330 --> 00:14:10.150
But it will be hot.

00:14:10.150 --> 00:14:12.980
Heat is the characteristic of fire;

00:14:12.980 --> 00:14:16.005
color is secondary.

00:14:16.005 --> 00:14:17.550
This is the second characteristic.  The

00:14:17.550 --> 00:14:19.870
second characteristic of fire

00:14:19.870 --> 00:14:22.950
is that it can be created by other forces.  The

00:14:22.950 --> 00:14:26.810
inherent properties of fire should originate from within.

00:14:26.810 --> 00:14:31.810
So no one can make fire hot,
but they can change its color

00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:35.500
by adding different chemical components.

00:14:35.500 --> 00:14:38.260
Everything about fire is

00:14:38.260 --> 00:14:40.647
contained in these two things.  It's

00:14:40.647 --> 00:14:44.630
either an inherent characteristic
or merely a feature;

00:14:44.630 --> 00:14:48.361
for example, color depends on other environmental factors.

00:14:49.369 --> 00:14:50.535
,GZHAN GYI DNGOS PO GA LA YOD, There's nothing

00:14:50.535 --> 00:14:52.906
else about fire.

00:14:52.906 --> 00:14:54.488
,GZHAN GYI DNGOS PO'I RANG BZHIN NI,

00:14:54.488 --> 00:14:57.138
,GZHAN GYI DNGOS PO YIN ZHES BRJOD,

00:15:00.218 --> 00:15:03.830
How can one say that what originates from elsewhere is one's true nature?

00:15:03.830 --> 00:15:05.960
When others believe that nature

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:09.810
originates from elsewhere, we say that what

00:15:09.810 --> 00:15:13.370
you are talking about exists independently.

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:14.970
--What's the meaning?

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:18.070
Does the color of fire depend on external factors?

00:15:18.070 --> 00:15:18.903
--Yes.

00:15:19.860 --> 00:15:21.810
But when you say that,

00:15:21.810 --> 00:15:24.910
you assume that chemical components create the color.  Do you

00:15:24.910 --> 00:15:25.743
understand?

00:15:28.259 --> 00:15:32.630
Is the color of fire
part of its innate characteristics?

00:15:32.630 --> 00:15:35.700
—No, it
changes depending on the chemical composition.

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:39.130
If you sprinkle chemicals into a fire, the
color of the fire will change; this change originates from

00:15:39.130 --> 00:15:42.460
external sources.  In

00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:43.833
other words, as you know, it's secondary.

00:15:43.833 --> 00:15:47.603
Created by external forces.

00:15:48.480 --> 00:15:52.290
But when you hear me say that,

00:15:52.290 --> 00:15:56.480
you assume it comes from chemical components, and
that's the problem.

00:15:56.480 --> 00:15:59.980
You even got the minor parts wrong.

00:16:00.967 --> 00:16:02.660
Forget that the heat of fire comes from itself; it

00:16:02.660 --> 00:16:04.290
doesn't.

00:16:04.290 --> 00:16:06.890
He is warm, and that warmth comes from you.

00:16:06.890 --> 00:16:09.520
Forget about that assumed characteristic.

00:16:09.520 --> 00:16:12.370
You even misunderstand why the color changed.

00:16:12.370 --> 00:16:14.887
You thought it was caused by chemical components.  Do you

00:16:15.740 --> 00:16:16.880
understand?

00:16:16.880 --> 00:16:19.420
By the way, that's all related to fire
.  That's all

00:16:19.420 --> 00:16:20.403
.  That

00:16:20.403 --> 00:16:22.905
's just how it is, and that's all there is to it.

00:16:23.949 --> 00:16:26.702
You know nothing about either of them.

00:16:28.071 --> 00:16:30.620
,RANG BZHIN DANG NI GZHAN DNGOS DAG,

00:16:30.620 --> 00:16:32.810
,MA GTOGS DNGOS PO GA LA YOD,

00:16:32.810 --> 00:16:36.860
Fire is its innate characteristic and the combination of its

00:16:36.860 --> 00:16:41.660
features created by external forces

00:16:41.660 --> 00:16:44.060
.

00:16:44.060 --> 00:16:46.450
There was no other fire besides that.

00:16:46.450 --> 00:16:48.950
Once these two points are included,
it constitutes the entirety of fire.

00:16:48.950 --> 00:16:50.530
But you don't understand either of them,

00:16:50.530 --> 00:16:53.900
therefore you don't understand fire.

00:16:53.900 --> 00:16:54.975
good.

00:16:54.975 --> 00:16:57.341
,RANG BZHIN DANG NI GZHAN DNGOS DAG,

00:16:57.341 --> 00:16:59.240
,YOD NA DNGOS PO 'GRUB PAR 'GYUR,

00:16:59.240 --> 00:17:00.413
in short.

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:03.550
Here he said, "

00:17:03.550 --> 00:17:05.830
You don't know RANG BZHIN

00:17:05.830 --> 00:17:08.100
and you don't know GZHAN DNGOS."

00:17:08.100 --> 00:17:11.460
You do not understand the basic nature of fire, its

00:17:11.460 --> 00:17:14.536
self-generating nature,
nor do you understand

00:17:14.536 --> 00:17:17.390
why it moves, why it
has different colors,

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:21.157
or why it has different temperatures.  You don't understand.

00:17:22.044 --> 00:17:25.323
,YOD NA DNGOS PO 'GRUB PAR 'GYUR,

00:17:25.323 --> 00:17:29.698
If the properties and characteristics of fire

00:17:29.698 --> 00:17:32.690
exist in the way you think they do,

00:17:32.690 --> 00:17:35.268
then it is not fire.

00:17:35.268 --> 00:17:37.130
,GAL TE DNGOS PO MA GRUB NA,

00:17:37.130 --> 00:17:39.788
If there were no real fire,

00:17:39.788 --> 00:17:42.170
,DNGOS MED 'GRUB PAR MI 'GYUR RO,

00:17:42.170 --> 00:17:47.170
then you would not have the
concept of unreal.

00:17:48.580 --> 00:17:53.580
Without real fire, it would be
difficult to define what is unreal.

00:17:54.010 --> 00:17:58.800
If there isn't real cream on the table
, then... it's

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:03.600
hard for my teacher to say
that it's fake cream.

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:05.480
Those powders are fake cream.

00:18:05.480 --> 00:18:09.420
If he had never seen
real cream, he couldn't...

00:18:09.420 --> 00:18:11.777
Real cream defines fake cream,

00:18:11.777 --> 00:18:14.960
and fake cream defines real cream.

00:18:14.960 --> 00:18:19.430
He didn't just smile and say, "Oh, real cream,"

00:18:19.430 --> 00:18:22.400
if he had never experienced the
danger of eating fake cream.

00:18:23.305 --> 00:18:24.200
[Laughter] I'm

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:28.270
always the one who has to convince the waiter to

00:18:28.270 --> 00:18:29.490
give him real cream.

00:18:29.490 --> 00:18:32.401
Good heavens, sometimes it takes half an hour.

00:18:35.357 --> 00:18:37.320
,DNGOS PO GZHAN DU GYUR PA NI, We've discussed this

00:18:37.320 --> 00:18:39.820
when things become something else

00:18:39.820 --> 00:18:41.300
.

00:18:41.300 --> 00:18:44.903
For example, when milk becomes yogurt,

00:18:45.956 --> 00:18:50.065
,DNGOS MED YIN PAR SKYE BO SMRA,

00:18:50.065 --> 00:18:51.840
SKYE BO SMRA means people say,

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:53.178
people in the world say.

00:18:53.178 --> 00:18:55.870
SKYE BO SMRA means what
people in the world would say.

00:18:55.870 --> 00:18:57.200
What would they say?

00:18:57.200 --> 00:18:59.791
This is not how it was originally.

00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:04.770
When milk is turned into yogurt,

00:19:04.770 --> 00:19:07.630
how do people talk about milk?

00:19:07.630 --> 00:19:10.363
They said this wasn't how it was supposed to be.  It

00:19:10.363 --> 00:19:15.345
's solid now, but it
was originally a liquid.

00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:26.763
If you can describe something as it was
originally,

00:19:26.763 --> 00:19:29.236
then it has no inherent nature.

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:33.460
It's not what it originally looked like.  It

00:19:33.460 --> 00:19:36.160
is not what it originally was, meaning that

00:19:36.160 --> 00:19:41.160
whatever changes, if it is not what it was, is
not its characteristic.

00:19:43.430 --> 00:19:45.023
Milk...

00:19:47.860 --> 00:19:50.243
When I look at yogurt, I mean milk.

00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:53.530
It is no longer milk.

00:19:53.530 --> 00:19:55.580
When you say it's no longer milk, you're referring

00:19:55.580 --> 00:19:58.380
to the characteristics of milk.  What

00:19:58.380 --> 00:20:00.970
is being said is that
characteristics will end and disappear.  It means that it

00:20:00.970 --> 00:20:03.500
can discard its characteristics.

00:20:03.500 --> 00:20:05.630
So it doesn't exist inside, right?

00:20:05.630 --> 00:20:08.050
So it must have originated from
somewhere else, right?

00:20:08.050 --> 00:20:10.290
Then it lacks inherent characteristics.

00:20:10.290 --> 00:20:12.910
All it has are features created by external forces
,

00:20:12.910 --> 00:20:16.440
such as the seeds in your consciousness.  Do you

00:20:16.440 --> 00:20:17.273
understand?

00:20:18.930 --> 00:20:19.763
good.

00:20:20.720 --> 00:20:22.763
Next, this photo shows real cream.

00:20:24.220 --> 00:20:26.022
I always see my teacher smiling

00:20:26.022 --> 00:20:28.605
whenever I see real cream.

00:20:30.209 --> 00:20:31.042
good.

00:20:32.541 --> 00:20:34.158
Let's look at the next passage.

00:20:35.034 --> 00:20:37.050
,GANG DAG RANG BZHIN GZHAN DNGOS DANG,

00:20:37.050 --> 00:20:39.158
,DNGOS DANG DNGOS MED NYID LTA BA,

00:20:39.158 --> 00:20:40.982
,DE DAG SANGS RGYAS BSTAN PA LA,

00:20:40.982 --> 00:20:43.441
,DE NYID MTHONG BA MA YIN NO,

00:20:45.280 --> 00:20:47.561
This is typical.......

00:20:52.496 --> 00:20:54.077
GANG DAG RANG BZHIN GZHAN DNGOS

00:20:54.077 --> 00:20:57.412
These are two things:
RANG BZHIN and GZHAN DNGOS.

00:20:58.260 --> 00:21:02.051
RANG BZHIN means
"his characteristics", innate characteristics.

00:21:02.051 --> 00:21:04.530
GZHAN DNGOS refers to its

00:21:04.530 --> 00:21:08.927
"additional features" that are
added due to the external environment.  Is

00:21:08.927 --> 00:21:12.160
DANG, DNGOS DANG DNGOS MED NYID LTA BA

00:21:12.160 --> 00:21:15.793
real or fake?

00:21:15.793 --> 00:21:19.720
Is this real cream or creamer?

00:21:20.930 --> 00:21:24.560
Is it something made from cows that
tastes delicious,

00:21:24.560 --> 00:21:29.483
or something created from flour?

00:21:29.483 --> 00:21:32.823
Here he makes two distinctions:

00:21:34.660 --> 00:21:39.660
characteristics and other variable features;

00:21:39.773 --> 00:21:44.040
real milk and fake milk.

00:21:44.940 --> 00:21:46.930
Two sets of differences, two distinct points.  The

00:21:46.930 --> 00:21:48.880
differences between the two groups.

00:21:48.880 --> 00:21:50.630
“When I describe it to you,”

00:21:50.630 --> 00:21:52.546
Nagarjuna said to another,

00:21:52.546 --> 00:21:55.957
“you still believe they exist on their own.” By the way,

00:21:55.957 --> 00:22:00.770
when I speak of truth or falsehood

00:22:00.770 --> 00:22:03.725
, I will ask you questions.  Is it true that

00:22:05.860 --> 00:22:09.191
reality can only be defined by unreality
?  Is it true that

00:22:12.920 --> 00:22:17.130
traits, innate traits, can only be
defined by changeable characteristics

00:22:17.130 --> 00:22:19.943
?

00:22:22.780 --> 00:22:25.730
In Buddhism, you need to see the short

00:22:25.730 --> 00:22:29.833
to understand the tall.

00:22:31.710 --> 00:22:34.750
Because many people will tell you that

00:22:34.750 --> 00:22:35.840
I always see this situation

00:22:35.840 --> 00:22:38.440
in some Burmese schools or American schools.

00:22:39.330 --> 00:22:42.040
They would say that emptiness is the

00:22:42.040 --> 00:22:45.313
result of comparison;

00:22:46.320 --> 00:22:48.650
nothing in itself is real
because it must be

00:22:48.650 --> 00:22:49.863
compared with other things.

00:22:49.863 --> 00:22:54.320
Is this emptiness?  Is this a
dependency origin?  No, that's not

00:22:54.320 --> 00:22:55.660
it.

00:22:55.660 --> 00:22:58.593
It has absolutely no relation to that.  The

00:22:58.593 --> 00:23:01.410
entire explanation of emptiness is ridiculous.

00:23:01.410 --> 00:23:03.030
Height is not defined by shortness;

00:23:03.030 --> 00:23:06.230
height depends on the seeds of height in your consciousness.

00:23:06.230 --> 00:23:07.390
It's that simple.

00:23:07.390 --> 00:23:09.760
You can still be tall even if you're not short,

00:23:09.760 --> 00:23:13.770
because the seed of height is in your consciousness, even if you're not short.

00:23:13.770 --> 00:23:15.290
Height does not depend on being short.

00:23:15.290 --> 00:23:18.386
It depends on what you did to someone yesterday.

00:23:18.386 --> 00:23:19.427
[Laughter] Do you

00:23:20.328 --> 00:23:21.210
understand?

00:23:21.210 --> 00:23:23.668
Things are not derived through comparison.

00:23:25.117 --> 00:23:27.980
Reality is not defined by human beings.

00:23:27.980 --> 00:23:31.190
In Buddhism, in true Buddhism,

00:23:31.190 --> 00:23:36.050
characteristics do not arise from temporary

00:23:36.050 --> 00:23:38.463
and changeable features.

00:23:39.350 --> 00:23:43.440
The characteristics depend on your seed.

00:23:44.770 --> 00:23:45.821
good.

00:23:45.821 --> 00:23:46.990


00:23:46.990 --> 00:23:51.990
If you believe that greatness is only great through comparison,

00:23:52.720 --> 00:23:57.720
or that characteristics are only characteristics through comparison of these accidental and changeable features, then

00:23:57.840 --> 00:24:00.710


00:24:00.710 --> 00:24:03.527
those who say this -- DE DAG

00:24:03.527 --> 00:24:04.985
SANGS RGYAS BSTAN PA LA, ,

00:24:04.985 --> 00:24:08.250
DE NYID MTHONG BA MA YIN They

00:24:08.250 --> 00:24:11.632
didn't MTHONG DE NYID -- tattva

00:24:13.934 --> 00:24:16.180
tattva

00:24:16.180 --> 00:24:19.019
Yeah, they didn't see emptiness, Yes,
they didn't see emptiness,

00:24:19.019 --> 00:24:21.375
DE BZHIN － So

00:24:21.375 --> 00:24:22.917
they didn't see............tattva means so.

00:24:22.917 --> 00:24:23.750
Here,

00:24:25.021 --> 00:24:28.220
if you believe that the nature of things, in a certain respect, can only be

00:24:28.220 --> 00:24:31.260
obtained through comparison, then you mean that you believe characteristics come

00:24:31.260 --> 00:24:34.320
from themselves, or characteristics come from the

00:24:34.320 --> 00:24:36.130
side of comparison.

00:24:36.130 --> 00:24:41.130
Then you don't understand the nature of things.

00:24:41.450 --> 00:24:43.520
This is a joke.  Do you understand?

00:24:43.520 --> 00:24:46.987
You do not understand the true nature of things.

00:24:46.987 --> 00:24:49.790
DE NYID -- The true nature of things.

00:24:49.790 --> 00:24:52.089
This is a joke.

00:24:52.089 --> 00:24:52.922
Okay?

00:24:54.030 --> 00:24:57.040
Incidentally, as the Buddhist teachings state,

00:24:57.040 --> 00:24:59.520
SANGS RGYAS BSTAN PA LA, line three,

00:24:59.520 --> 00:25:02.600
you do not understand the Dharma.

00:25:02.600 --> 00:25:05.190
Then, I don't know why

00:25:05.190 --> 00:25:07.638
I found this picture for everyone:

00:25:10.830 --> 00:25:13.870
three people wearing blindfolds.

00:25:13.870 --> 00:25:16.250


00:25:16.250 --> 00:25:20.830


00:25:20.830 --> 00:25:23.370
They seem to be wandering in darkness because they have a wrong concept of characteristics or self-existence.

00:25:23.370 --> 00:25:26.550
I just wanted you to see this picture

00:25:26.550 --> 00:25:31.550
because I want you to be grateful
for why Nagarjuna Bodhisattva

00:25:32.470 --> 00:25:36.550
repeatedly said,
"They didn't understand the Buddha's teachings."

00:25:36.550 --> 00:25:38.270
"They didn't understand the Buddha's teachings."

00:25:38.270 --> 00:25:40.120
Historically, why did he seem

00:25:40.120 --> 00:25:43.465
particularly concerned about this?  One hundred US dollars!

00:25:43.465 --> 00:25:45.152
[Female voice, inaudible]

00:25:45.152 --> 00:25:47.706
— Historically, historically

00:25:53.250 --> 00:25:56.684
[female voice, inaudible]

00:25:56.684 --> 00:25:59.000
Why does he repeatedly return to this topic:

00:25:59.000 --> 00:26:01.525
"You did not understand the Buddha's teachings."

00:26:01.525 --> 00:26:04.266
— [Venerable Jigme] Perhaps because [inaudible]

00:26:05.870 --> 00:26:09.717
— Very good, $50 is now available.

00:26:09.717 --> 00:26:14.026
Jigme said that there was another system that contradicted his teachings—

00:26:14.026 --> 00:26:15.330
[Jigme] and it was the prevailing system

00:26:15.330 --> 00:26:17.935
—for how long?  Fifty US dollars

00:26:17.935 --> 00:26:19.444
— [Jigme] Two hundred years

00:26:19.444 --> 00:26:20.611
— Seven hundred years

00:26:20.611 --> 00:26:22.069
— [Jigme] Abhidharma

00:26:22.069 --> 00:26:23.168
— Yes, Abhidharma

00:26:23.168 --> 00:26:26.526
People have misunderstood for seven hundred years.

00:26:27.590 --> 00:26:29.380
They quoted the Buddha.  Recite the Buddha's words.

00:26:29.380 --> 00:26:30.780
They can memorize them.

00:26:30.780 --> 00:26:32.620
They can recite all the scriptures.

00:26:32.620 --> 00:26:35.311
And according to Professor Nick's verses, the

00:26:35.311 --> 00:26:37.477
Buddha kept it, you know.  ．  ．

00:26:38.889 --> 00:26:43.803
Emptiness is also described in Abhidharma texts.

00:26:43.803 --> 00:26:48.470
Nagarjuna proved this in the Sixty Verses, which also discusses emptiness in

00:26:49.600 --> 00:26:53.090
Theravada Buddhist scriptures.


00:26:53.090 --> 00:26:54.670
He proved this point,

00:26:54.670 --> 00:26:57.560
so one can imagine how frustrated Nagarjuna must have been.

00:26:57.560 --> 00:27:01.670
He resisted seven hundred years of misunderstanding.

00:27:01.670 --> 00:27:03.740
He tried to stand alone

00:27:03.740 --> 00:27:07.860
before a seven-hundred-year-old wave, saying,

00:27:07.860 --> 00:27:12.343
"Hey everyone, this is all wrong!"
[Imitations came wave after wave.]

00:27:13.350 --> 00:27:15.520
Therefore, he had to constantly return to the classics and

00:27:15.520 --> 00:27:17.640
say, "You don't understand,"

00:27:17.640 --> 00:27:19.560
"You didn't get it."

00:27:19.560 --> 00:27:20.690
This was not what he meant.

00:27:20.690 --> 00:27:22.320
Understand?

00:27:22.320 --> 00:27:27.244
Can't you hear the seven hundred years of frustration in his voice?

00:27:27.244 --> 00:27:28.077
Okay, so

00:27:28.077 --> 00:27:31.060
this is what it means to have your eyes covered.  It will remind you once again that it is extremely important for

00:27:34.370 --> 00:27:38.090
us to now switch to
a key point in Buddhism

00:27:38.090 --> 00:27:40.020
.

00:27:40.020 --> 00:27:41.290
I'm sorry, this last class today is

00:27:41.290 --> 00:27:43.153
only halfway through

00:27:43.153 --> 00:27:46.146
because everyone is very tired, but let's continue.

00:27:46.146 --> 00:27:48.179
,BCOM LDAN DNGOS DANG DNGOS MED PA,

00:27:48.179 --> 00:27:50.895
,MKHYEN PAS KA TA YA NA YI,

00:27:50.895 --> 00:27:52.820
,GDAM NGAG LAS NI YOD PA DANG,

00:27:52.820 --> 00:27:55.530
,MED PA GNYIS KA'ANG DGAG PA MDZAD,

00:27:55.530 --> 00:27:57.133
Very, very Nagarjuna.

00:27:58.170 --> 00:28:00.080
Very important.

00:28:00.080 --> 00:28:04.995
For the two husbands in the kitchen,

00:28:04.995 --> 00:28:09.590
BCOM DAS—Bhagavan—Buddha said

00:28:09.590 --> 00:28:11.772
he understood MKHYEN PA.

00:28:11.772 --> 00:28:14.266
Buddha knew the

00:28:14.266 --> 00:28:15.708
difference between DNGOS and DNGOS MED.

00:28:15.708 --> 00:28:19.624
Here, DNGOS and DNGOS MED
refer to the real and the unreal. The

00:28:21.751 --> 00:28:22.968
Buddha understood the

00:28:22.968 --> 00:28:24.680
difference between the real and the unreal.  The

00:28:24.680 --> 00:28:26.850
real husband in the kitchen,

00:28:26.850 --> 00:28:28.530
and the fake husband in the kitchen.

00:28:28.530 --> 00:28:30.380
He was aware of this difference.

00:28:30.380 --> 00:28:34.230
In the *Katyayana Sutra*,

00:28:34.230 --> 00:28:37.520
this is one of his beloved disciples.

00:28:37.520 --> 00:28:39.220
Katyayana is

00:28:39.220 --> 00:28:44.220


00:28:44.380 --> 00:28:47.100
very important in the scriptures related to the Wheel of Life.

00:28:47.100 --> 00:28:50.780
He personally witnessed the first drawing of the Wheel of Life, and

00:28:50.780 --> 00:28:54.010
then returned home to tell the story.

00:28:54.010 --> 00:28:58.070
In short, the Buddha gave Katyayana personal advice.

00:28:58.070 --> 00:29:00.727
I specifically looked for it, and

00:29:00.727 --> 00:29:03.241
you found some, but it wasn't clear enough.

00:29:03.241 --> 00:29:05.516
LAS NI YOD PA DANG MED PA
GNYIS KA'ANG DGAG PA MDZAD

00:29:05.516 --> 00:29:07.747
The Buddha denies the possibility of things existing, and

00:29:07.747 --> 00:29:12.747
at the same time, the Buddha also denies the possibility of things not existing.

00:29:13.163 --> 00:29:15.590
The Buddha denied the existence of things, and at

00:29:15.590 --> 00:29:18.610
the same time denied that things could not exist.

00:29:18.610 --> 00:29:19.530
Okay?

00:29:19.530 --> 00:29:22.000
This is something that Nagarjuna Bodhisattva repeatedly emphasized as

00:29:22.000 --> 00:29:23.760
extremely important.  It's

00:29:23.760 --> 00:29:27.710
especially helpful for understanding the two husbands in the kitchen.

00:29:27.710 --> 00:29:32.710
A reward of one hundred dollars.  In the kitchen,

00:29:34.640 --> 00:29:38.010
where is the existence of things denied,
and where is the non-existence of things denied?  You need to

00:29:38.010 --> 00:29:40.456
answer both correctly to win the $100 reward.

00:29:42.170 --> 00:29:44.090
What exists in the kitchen,

00:29:44.090 --> 00:29:46.307
and what does not?

00:29:48.735 --> 00:29:49.848
—[Jimei] The husband you created.
 
596
00:29:49,848 --&gt; 00:29:51,703
——The husband you created does exist.

00:29:51.703 --> 00:29:52.961
—[Master Jimei] The husband you did not create.

00:29:52.961 --> 00:29:55.988
— Yes, the husband who said it wasn't my fault doesn't exist.  The statement that

00:29:55.988 --> 00:29:59.440
something does not exist is actually true; this

00:29:59.440 --> 00:30:02.330
is called the extreme of existence.  The

00:30:02.330 --> 00:30:06.683
non-existence of what is said to truly exist

00:30:06.683 --> 00:30:09.050
is called the extreme of non-existence.

00:30:09.050 --> 00:30:10.773
You've gone too far.

00:30:13.107 --> 00:30:15.900
If the husband in the kitchen isn't my fault
, then he

00:30:15.900 --> 00:30:16.790
doesn't exist.

00:30:16.790 --> 00:30:17.890
Feel sorry.

00:30:17.890 --> 00:30:20.420
If it weren't for the husband in the kitchen's fault,

00:30:20.420 --> 00:30:22.020
he wouldn't exist at all.  Do you

00:30:23.345 --> 00:30:24.536
understand?

00:30:26.041 --> 00:30:27.180
[Female voice, unclear]

00:30:27.180 --> 00:30:32.180
And because the husband in the kitchen is my fault,
he does exist.

00:30:32.780 --> 00:30:36.380
Therefore, at the same time, this husband both exists and does
not exist.

00:30:36.380 --> 00:30:38.673
Denying his existence is a problem.  It's wrong to

00:30:39.680 --> 00:30:43.543
deny the existence of a husband who is at fault
.

00:30:44.580 --> 00:30:46.280
At the same time, it is

00:30:46.280 --> 00:30:48.313
also wrong to deny the presence of any husband in the kitchen.  Do you

00:30:49.150 --> 00:30:50.510
understand?

00:30:50.510 --> 00:30:51.550
Two extremes.

00:30:51.550 --> 00:30:53.230
We call it a cliff fall.

00:30:53.230 --> 00:30:56.529
Actually, this diagram

00:30:56.529 --> 00:31:00.770
is a crossing...

00:31:00.770 --> 00:31:02.500
I was trying to find a bridge in Arizona.

00:31:02.500 --> 00:31:03.363
Good luck.

00:31:05.690 --> 00:31:07.760
This is called the Middle Way.

00:31:07.760 --> 00:31:10.710
And you try to traverse between

00:31:10.710 --> 00:31:12.820
non-existence and existence.

00:31:12.820 --> 00:31:15.960
If you believe that a husband who isn't at fault truly exists,

00:31:15.960 --> 00:31:18.200
then you've fallen to one side.

00:31:18.200 --> 00:31:21.220
If you think you don't have a husband.

00:31:21.220 --> 00:31:23.700
Then you fall to the other side.

00:31:23.700 --> 00:31:27.400
This is the most

00:31:27.400 --> 00:31:29.250
important source of this concept in all Buddhist scriptures.  This

00:31:29.250 --> 00:31:31.493
is the place.  yeah.

00:31:31.493 --> 00:31:32.326


00:31:33.810 --> 00:31:34.643
OK

00:31:34.643 --> 00:31:38.870
This also means now is a
good time to take a Sanskrit lesson.

