00:40:47.482 --> 00:40:51.000
If you believe things exist,
then you fall into the extreme idea that things can never be changed.

00:40:51.000 --> 00:40:54.330


00:40:54.330 --> 00:40:56.530
If you believe things don't exist,

00:40:56.530 --> 00:40:59.973
then you fall into the extreme idea that things never came into being.


00:41:00.870 --> 00:41:05.870
Therefore, you great masters

00:41:06.680 --> 00:41:09.170
should remain in the middle

00:41:09.170 --> 00:41:11.740
. Hence, there is Madhyamika.

00:41:11.740 --> 00:41:14.415
What is another name for wisdom?

00:41:16.510 --> 00:41:18.861
Yes, Madhyamika.

00:41:18.861 --> 00:41:20.540
Madhyamika.

00:41:20.540 --> 00:41:24.100
This is another name for Prajna.

00:41:24.100 --> 00:41:27.825
Where have you seen this other name?
A hundred-dollar bounty

00:41:29.164 --> 00:41:32.997
[Christina] Lama Chuni's… title
[weak voice]

00:41:35.050 --> 00:41:36.828
Pretty close

00:41:36.828 --> 00:41:37.900
— [Tim] Madhyamaka

00:41:37.900 --> 00:41:40.832
— Yes, Tim got a hundred dollars.

00:41:40.832 --> 00:41:43.120
A hundred dollars for Tim.

00:41:43.120 --> 00:41:43.953
Okay,

00:41:45.240 --> 00:41:48.930
Chandrakirti didn't
name his book Madhyamika.

00:41:48.930 --> 00:41:51.200
He named it Madhyamaka.

00:41:51.200 --> 00:41:55.850
This one related to Madhyamika is
called Madhyamaka. A

00:41:55.850 --> 00:41:58.180
commentary on Madhyamika.

00:41:58.180 --> 00:41:59.013
Okay.

00:41:59.013 --> 00:42:00.310
Here,

00:42:00.310 --> 00:42:05.310
if you believe things exist,
then they can never change.

00:42:05.750 --> 00:42:09.413
If you believe things don't exist,
then you are a nihilist.

00:42:10.800 --> 00:42:11.633
Okay?

00:42:11.633 --> 00:42:16.625
Therefore, a true wise person

00:42:17.602 --> 00:42:20.070
should remain between the two views.

00:42:20.070 --> 00:42:22.790
You should be between the two views.

00:42:22.790 --> 00:42:25.541
What does this mean in the context of the kitchen? Three hundred dollars!

00:42:26.600 --> 00:42:27.780
[Pau] I understand…

00:42:27.780 --> 00:42:28.810
— Slow down, slow down.

00:42:28.810 --> 00:42:30.311
That's a lot of money.

00:42:30.311 --> 00:42:32.110
[Laughter]

00:42:32.110 --> 00:42:33.880
What is the middle ground in the kitchen?

00:42:33.880 --> 00:42:38.880
— [Pau] When you realize
your husband is yelling at you

00:42:39.263 --> 00:42:44.254
because you yelled at the kids last week
.

00:42:45.169 --> 00:42:46.252
— Good.

00:42:47.457 --> 00:42:50.307
So, that exists.

00:42:50.307 --> 00:42:52.312
Then what doesn't exist in the kitchen?

00:42:52.312 --> 00:42:56.253
— [Pau] That "I didn't do anything"
husband.

00:42:56.253 --> 00:42:59.222
— That "I didn't do anything"
husband doesn't exist, yes.

00:42:59.222 --> 00:43:01.230
So, stay in the middle.

00:43:01.230 --> 00:43:02.607
Understand?

00:43:02.607 --> 00:43:05.178
Three hundred dollars.

00:43:05.178 --> 00:43:07.180
[Exhale]

00:43:07.180 --> 00:43:09.499
Pudge, she'll treat you to a big meal.

00:43:09.499 --> 00:43:10.514
Okay?

00:43:10.514 --> 00:43:12.516
[Someone's voice, unclear]

00:43:12.516 --> 00:43:14.300
Good.

00:43:14.300 --> 00:43:15.849
,GANG ZHIG RANG BZHIN GYIS YOD PA, ,

00:43:15.849 --> 00:43:17.815
DE NI MED PA MIN PAS RTAG,

00:43:17.815 --> 00:43:20.389
,SNGON BYUNG DA LTAR MED CES PA,

00:43:20.389 --> 00:43:22.897
,DES NA CHAD PAR THAL BAR 'GYUR.

00:43:22.897 --> 00:43:23.730
Okay.

00:43:23.730 --> 00:43:24.840
Then he extended the

00:43:24.840 --> 00:43:29.570
meaning of immutability and never beginning.

00:43:29.570 --> 00:43:33.710
Incidentally, these two extremes,

00:43:33.710 --> 00:43:38.710
immutability and cessation,  This


00:43:39.080 --> 00:43:42.610
refers to the result of a specific argument.

00:43:42.610 --> 00:43:45.560
They are described as the
result of a specific argument.

00:43:46.440 --> 00:43:51.405
If the husband
comes from his own side,

00:43:52.930 --> 00:43:56.286
he will never change—RTAG PA.

00:43:56.286 --> 00:43:59.579
So what about the other one?

00:43:59.579 --> 00:44:01.380
CHAD PA.

00:44:01.380 --> 00:44:04.710
I think if he comes from, and

00:44:04.710 --> 00:44:09.510
if he doesn't come from his own side,
he doesn't exist.

00:44:09.510 --> 00:44:11.763
Then he must stop.

00:44:13.248 --> 00:44:14.807
Understand?

00:44:15.730 --> 00:44:16.563
Okay.

00:44:16.563 --> 00:44:20.573
And then I have a
picture I made especially for you. The

00:44:21.410 --> 00:44:26.165
Middle Way about the two husbands,

00:44:29.136 --> 00:44:29.969
okay?

00:44:30.885 --> 00:44:34.350
If you think he only comes
from his own side,

00:44:34.350 --> 00:44:37.228
you fall to the right side of the bridge.

00:44:37.228 --> 00:44:39.470
If you think that if he
doesn't come from his own side,

00:44:39.470 --> 00:44:42.790
he can't exist,
then you fall to the left side of the bridge.

00:44:42.790 --> 00:44:45.210
If you stop at the Middle Way,

00:44:45.210 --> 00:44:47.508
you have a happy relationship.

00:44:48.561 --> 00:44:49.417
Yay!

00:44:52.650 --> 00:44:54.010
Oh, sorry,

00:44:54.010 --> 00:44:57.491
this is the last picture for this lesson.

00:44:57.491 --> 00:44:59.520
So let's summarize.

00:44:59.520 --> 00:45:01.690
What is this chapter called?

00:45:01.690 --> 00:45:04.330
We explored characteristics.

00:45:04.330 --> 00:45:08.690
Do things have inherent existence?

00:45:08.690 --> 00:45:13.690
The conclusion is that things do not have inherent existence.

00:45:14.250 --> 00:45:18.370
Because even if things have characteristics,

00:45:18.370 --> 00:45:21.890
like the heat of fire, seemingly
in the fire, it

00:45:21.890 --> 00:45:24.010
also comes from us.

00:45:24.010 --> 00:45:25.460
That's the bottom line.

00:45:25.460 --> 00:45:28.560
So things have no inherent existence.

00:45:29.670 --> 00:45:30.503
Okay.

00:45:30.503 --> 00:45:33.867
What does that mean in relation to the Medicine Buddha mantra?

00:45:35.173 --> 00:45:36.300
[Woman's voice, unclear]

00:45:36.300 --> 00:45:38.658
Yes, what happens if you

00:45:38.658 --> 00:45:41.000
chant the Medicine Buddha mantra with bad intentions

00:45:41.000 --> 00:45:42.150
?

00:45:42.150 --> 00:45:43.663
The characteristics of this mantra

00:45:44.700 --> 00:45:47.470
will manifest.

00:45:47.470 --> 00:45:50.803
Are there any beneficial characteristics?

00:45:51.760 --> 00:45:52.969
No.

00:45:52.969 --> 00:45:56.350
If you
chant these mantras with a competitive mindset,

00:45:56.350 --> 00:45:58.270
then these mantras will harm people, okay?

00:45:58.270 --> 00:45:59.103
Cool, right?

00:45:59.103 --> 00:46:01.450
That's the emptiness of these mantras.

00:46:01.450 --> 00:46:04.243
They are without inherent existence.

00:46:05.680 --> 00:46:06.513
Cool.

00:46:06.513 --> 00:46:08.738
See you next time! Yay!

